---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SupportEmail from '../../components/SupportEmail.astro';

const title = 'Support — Keyboard Studio';
const description =
  'Set up Keyboard Studio, enable Full Access optionally, troubleshoot click sound and haptics, and learn about phrases, dictionary, and layouts.';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/support/">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Keyboard Studio Support</h1>
      <p>
        Setup guides and troubleshooting for Keyboard Studio on iPhone and iPad.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow prose" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
      <p class="toc__title" id="toc-heading">On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#enable">Enable Keyboard Studio</a></li>
        <li><a href="#full-access">Enable Full Access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#click-sound">Keyboard click sound</a></li>
        <li><a href="#haptics">Haptics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#quick-phrases">Quick Phrases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#personal-dictionary">Personal Dictionary</a></li>
        <li><a href="#local-candidates">Local Candidates</a></li>
        <li><a href="#autocorrection">Local Autocorrection</a></li>
        <li><a href="#emoji">Local Emoji Search</a></li>
        <li><a href="#swipe">Swipe Typing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#long-press">Long-press alternate characters</a></li>
        <li><a href="#spacebar">Spacebar cursor movement</a></li>
        <li><a href="#one-handed">One-handed layouts</a></li>
        <li><a href="#ipad">iPad adaptive layout</a></li>
        <li><a href="#photo-background">Photo Background</a></li>
        <li><a href="#safe-defaults">Restore Safe Defaults</a></li>
        <li><a href="#globe">Switch keyboards with Globe</a></li>
        <li><a href="#full-access-faq">Full Access privacy FAQ</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact support</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="enable">1. Enable Keyboard Studio</h2>
    <p>Add Keyboard Studio as a system keyboard:</p>
    <div class="support-steps" role="group" aria-label="Enable Keyboard Studio steps">
      Settings<br />
      → General<br />
      → Keyboard<br />
      → Keyboards<br />
      → Add New Keyboard<br />
      → Keyboard Studio
    </div>
    <p>
      After adding the keyboard, open any text field, tap and hold the Globe key
      (or use the keyboard switcher), and choose Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="full-access">2. Enable Full Access</h2>
    <p>
      Full Access is optional. Without Full Access, basic typing works, the bundled
      offline lexicon works, gestures and layouts work, and safe defaults are
      available.
    </p>
    <p>With Full Access enabled:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Settings saved in the containing App may synchronize through the local App
        Group container
      </li>
      <li>
        Quick Phrases and Personal Dictionary created in the App may be available
        to the keyboard
      </li>
      <li>
        System keyboard click audio may be available when enabled
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      iOS grants third-party keyboards additional capabilities when Allow Full
      Access is enabled. Keyboard Studio uses Full Access where applicable for
      supported local App Group sharing and iOS keyboard feedback. Enabling it does
      not change Keyboard Studio’s privacy practices or cause the App to upload
      typed text, swipe paths, Emoji searches, Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary
      entries, photos, or settings. It does not activate accounts, advertising, or
      analytics.
    </p>
    <p>
      To enable Full Access, open
      <strong>Settings → General → Keyboard → Keyboards → Keyboard Studio</strong>
      and turn on Allow Full Access.
    </p>

    <h2 id="click-sound">3. Keyboard click sound troubleshooting</h2>
    <p>If click sound is missing or inconsistent, check these steps:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Enable Keyboard Feedback Sound in iOS Settings.</li>
      <li>Enable System Click Sound in Keyboard Studio.</li>
      <li>Save settings in Keyboard Studio.</li>
      <li>Enable Full Access for Keyboard Studio.</li>
      <li>
        Remove and re-add the keyboard, or restart the Extension session where
        needed.
      </li>
      <li>Confirm the Apple keyboard produces sound on your device.</li>
      <li>
        Note that custom-keyboard click loudness may differ from the Apple
        keyboard.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not install custom audio files for this feature. Keyboard Studio uses
      supported iOS public system feedback facilities when available. Custom-keyboard
      feedback may differ from Apple’s system keyboard.
    </p>

    <h2 id="haptics">4. Haptics troubleshooting</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio offers configurable haptic feedback, including Light, Medium,
      and Strong settings. Physical feedback varies by device model, system haptic
      settings, and whether haptics are supported on that hardware. If feedback
      feels weak or absent, confirm system haptics are enabled and try a different
      intensity in Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="quick-phrases">5. Quick Phrases</h2>
    <p>
      Create Quick Phrases in the Keyboard Studio App. Phrases are stored locally.
      With Full Access enabled, phrases created in the App may become available to
      the Keyboard Extension through the local App Group container.
    </p>

    <h2 id="personal-dictionary">6. Personal Dictionary</h2>
    <p>
      Add words to your Personal Dictionary in the App. Entries remain local. With
      Full Access enabled, dictionary entries created in the App may be available
      to the keyboard through the local App Group container.
    </p>

    <h2 id="local-candidates">7. Local Candidates</h2>
    <p>
      Local word candidates are generated on-device. They do not require a network
      connection and are not uploaded by Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="autocorrection">8. Local Autocorrection</h2>
    <p>
      Bundled autocorrection is optional and off by default. When enabled, it works
      locally using on-device resources, including the bundled offline lexicon.
    </p>

    <h2 id="emoji">9. Local Emoji Search</h2>
    <p>
      Emoji search uses a bundled catalog and local search information. Search text
      is matched on-device and is not sent to a Keyboard Studio server.
    </p>

    <h2 id="swipe">10. Swipe Typing</h2>
    <p>
      Supported swipe typing is processed on-device. Keyboard Studio does not upload
      swipe paths or use a remote account to learn your typing behavior.
    </p>

    <h2 id="long-press">11. Long-press alternate characters</h2>
    <p>
      Press and hold a key to access alternate characters where available, then
      slide to the character you want and release.
    </p>

    <h2 id="spacebar">12. Spacebar cursor movement</h2>
    <p>
      Slide on the spacebar to move the cursor. This gesture works as part of the
      keyboard’s local input controls.
    </p>

    <h2 id="one-handed">13. One-handed layouts</h2>
    <p>
      Choose left or right one-handed layouts to bring keys closer for single-hand
      typing. You can switch back to the standard layout at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ipad">14. iPad adaptive layout</h2>
    <p>
      On iPad, Keyboard Studio provides adaptive layouts intended to fit common
      iPad typing arrangements. Layout availability depends on your device and
      orientation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="photo-background">15. Photo Background</h2>
    <p>
      Choose a photo through Apple’s system photo-selection interface. Keyboard
      Studio processes and stores the keyboard-background copy locally. You can
      change, re-crop, or remove it in the App; it is not uploaded to a Keyboard
      Studio server.
    </p>

    <h2 id="safe-defaults">16. Restore Safe Defaults</h2>
    <p>
      If settings become confusing or typing behavior feels unexpected, use Restore
      Safe Defaults in Keyboard Studio. This returns configurable options to a
      known-safe baseline while leaving your decision about Full Access under your
      control in iOS Settings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="globe">17. Switch keyboards with Globe</h2>
    <p>
      Tap the Globe key, or tap and hold it, to switch between Keyboard Studio and
      other keyboards installed on your device.
    </p>

    <h2 id="full-access-faq">18. Full Access privacy FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Does Full Access upload what I type?</h3>
    <p>
      No. iOS grants additional capabilities when Full Access is enabled, but
      Keyboard Studio does not use them to upload what you type or other local
      keyboard data.
    </p>
    <h3>What does Full Access allow?</h3>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio may use it for supported local configuration sharing between
      the App and Keyboard Extension through Apple’s App Group mechanism and for
      supported iOS keyboard feedback where applicable.
    </p>
    <h3>Is Full Access required?</h3>
    <p>
      No. Without Full Access, basic typing, the bundled offline lexicon, gestures,
      layouts, and safe defaults remain available.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">19. Contact support</h2>
    <p>
      Email <SupportEmail subject="Keyboard Studio Support" /> for Keyboard Studio
      support. You may send questions, bug reports, or feedback.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no contact form or ticket system on this site. Use email directly.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
